{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788969902,"nonce":"5X4YLkP1bHIBVesS2qKLlhlAPXY=","title":"nepo-restock verb: Nepo's standing restock rules are unreachable","message":"`nepo-order` places one-shot orders only. Nepo itself carries standing restock rules and the bridge binds none of them, so an agent that wants a stock level maintained must re-order by hand forever.\n\n## What exists in Nepo and is not bound\n\n`Nepo/RestockOrder` — `def`, `threshold` (\"restock at\"), `target` (\"restock to\"), `enabled`, `stuff`, `color`.\n`NepoGameComponent.SetRestock(def, threshold, target, enabled, stuff, color)`, `.GetRestock(def)`, `.AllRestocks`, swept by `.RunRestockSweep()` on the component tick.\nThe synced entry point is `NepoSync.SetRestockRule`, which is what the catalog window's customize panel calls.\n\n`NepoBridge` binds `requireCommsForRestock` (read) and nothing else on this surface. `nepo-inbound` reports `pendingDispatches`, which are the *output* of the sweep, so the agent can see restocks arriving that it has no way to create.\n\n## Why it matters beyond convenience\n\n`requireCommsForRestock` defaults true, so a standing rule queues a dispatch that a colonist must call in at a comms console — a real in-game act with a work giver behind it (`WorkGiver_DispatchRestockOrder`). That is a richer play surface than a one-shot order and it is currently invisible to the agent except as an alert it cannot cause.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `nepo-restock` reads and writes standing rules: no args lists every rule (`def`, `threshold`, `target`, `enabled`, `stuff`); with `def` + `threshold` + `target` it sets one; `enabled:false` disables while keeping the numbers, matching `SetRestock`'s own semantics; removing is whatever `SetRestock` does with a zeroed rule (read it, do not invent).\n- It routes through `NepoSync.SetRestockRule` so the write is a synced command, never `SetRestock` directly.\n- `stuff` round-trips: a rule set with a stuff delivers in that stuff.\n- The verb is soft-dependency only, through `NepoBridge`, and answers `gate:\"nepo-absent\"` on a bench without Nepo like the other three.\n- `dry_run` previews without writing, matching `nepo-order`.\n- A rule whose threshold is crossed produces a dispatch visible in `nepo-inbound`, closing the loop the agent can currently only observe.","files":null}]}